---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
---

<Legal
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="How AgentOS subscription refunds and cancellations work through Paddle."
  path="/refunds"
  updated="Effective September 7, 2026."
>
  <h2>Merchant of Record</h2>
  <p>
    AgentOS subscription orders processed through Paddle are sold and processed
    by Paddle.com as Merchant of Record. Paddle handles payment processing,
    applicable transaction taxes, buyer billing support, and the processing of
    eligible refunds.
  </p>

  <h2>Refund eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    Unless a refund or withdrawal right is required by applicable law, or is
    available under Paddle's buyer terms and refund rules, completed
    subscription charges are generally non-refundable. Refund requests may be
    reviewed based on the circumstances, including duplicate charges, material
    service defects, or other situations recognized by applicable law or
    Paddle's policies.
  </p>

  <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Start by contacting <a href="/support">AgentOS Support</a> with the account
    email and transaction details. Do not send full card numbers, passwords, API
    keys, or other sensitive credentials. Buyers may also use the billing or
    support links supplied by Paddle in their receipt or subscription-management
    communications.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancellations</h2>
  <p>
    You may cancel a recurring subscription to stop future renewal charges.
    Unless applicable law or an approved refund provides otherwise, cancellation
    does not automatically refund a charge that has already been completed.
    Access ordinarily continues through the end of the paid subscription period,
    subject to the applicable plan terms and provider status.
  </p>

  <h2>Service issues</h2>
  <p>
    If a material technical problem prevents access to the purchased AgentOS
    service, contact support so we can attempt to resolve it. Where a refund is
    approved or legally required, it will be processed through the payment
    provider rather than by requesting card or bank details from the buyer.
  </p>

  <h2>Mandatory consumer rights</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in this policy limits any non-waivable consumer rights that apply in
    the buyer's jurisdiction. Where mandatory law provides greater rights, those
    rights apply.
  </p>
</Legal>
